Keep the pinned Fastlane benchmark reproducible without changing its 3,613
selected examples. Backport the upstream token-time adjustment [1].

Legacy CBC checks padding rather than authenticating the password. A random
salt can give the wrong key valid padding [2]. Use a known invalid fixture
for this error path while running the real encryption and decryption.

[1]: https://github.com/fastlane/fastlane/commit/2beac83f8
[2]: https://github.com/fastlane/fastlane/issues/21663

diff --git a/spaceship/lib/spaceship/connect_api/token.rb b/spaceship/lib/spaceship/connect_api/token.rb
--- a/spaceship/lib/spaceship/connect_api/token.rb
+++ b/spaceship/lib/spaceship/connect_api/token.rb
@@ -102,3 +102,4 @@
           iss: issuer_id,
-          iat: now.to_i,
+          # Reduce the issued-at-time in case our time is slighly ahead of Apple's servers, which causes the token to be rejected.
+          iat: now.to_i - 60,
           exp: @expiration.to_i,
diff --git a/spaceship/spec/connect_api/token_spec.rb b/spaceship/spec/connect_api/token_spec.rb
--- a/spaceship/spec/connect_api/token_spec.rb
+++ b/spaceship/spec/connect_api/token_spec.rb
@@ -217,3 +217,3 @@
       expect(payload['iss']).to eq(issuer_id)
-      expect(payload['iat']).to eq(Time.now.to_i)
+      expect(payload['iat']).to be < Time.now.to_i
       expect(payload['aud']).to eq('appstoreconnect-v1')
diff --git a/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb b/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb
--- a/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb
+++ b/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
     end
 
     it "raises an exception if invalid password is passed" do
+      # Keep the legacy CBC error-path fixture deterministic.
+      allow(SecureRandom).to receive(:random_bytes).with(8).and_return("\0" * 8)
       @e.encrypt_files
       expect(File.read(@full_path)).to_not(eq(@content))
 
